{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 66, :comments ["<b>Your life shall hang in doubt before you.</b> On uncertainty — every uncertainty is called תָּלוּי: perhaps I shall die today by the sword that comes upon us. And our Sages interpreted this as referring to one who buys grain from the market." "<b>And you shall not trust in your life.</b> This is one who relies on the פַּלְטֵר (cf. Menachot 103)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {1 "פַּלְטֵר — likely from Greek/Late Latin pistor, 'baker,' referring to one who depends on the baker for daily bread; Rashi cites Menachot 103b where this derashah appears."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:45.783552493Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}